id: key-grammar-malformed-line-reject
category: key-grammar
images: rs-oracle10
targets: rhel10
key: NONE
xfail_issue: 
comment: the REJECT side of the corpus-wide two-sided positive control: a bare non-assignment line ('this is not valid', no '='). The real oracle logs a parse rejection ('Line is not an assignment, ignoring') and exits nonzero; RuleSteward emits sysctld-F01 for the same line. If a corpus capture ever shows NO reject-signal anywhere, the ORACLE-BROKEN guard fires.
